# The M1 regression baseline (ADR-0014). `make test` exits 0 only when the
# set of tests that do NOT pass matches this file exactly, so this is a
# working regression gate against the current core. Lines come out one at a
# time, in the same commit as the fix that makes that test pass — the
# deletion is the evidence the fix worked. This file is never regenerated
# wholesale from a run (that would launder a regression into the baseline);
# edit it by hand, and justify any line added back in the PR that adds it.
#
# JEF-607 (ADR-0004/ADR-0009: combinational-read regfile + write-through
# bypass, valid bits, the stall-only hazard interlock, and the divider's
# stall wired up for real) took this to empty: all 47 tests in the suite
# (including test/asm/hazard.S, added by that same ticket) genuinely pass.
# It stays here, empty, so the set-equality check below keeps working as the
# plain all-pass gate ADR-0014 describes for this state.
#
# JEF-628 (RVFI driven, test/monitor.v compiled into the cxxrtl leg for
# real, per-retire checking) reintroduces two: div.S and rem.S now fail
# under the monitor, but NOT because of anything wrong in this core's
# division/remainder arithmetic (test/exec_tb.v's >=10,000-vector
# differential bench and the executor's arithmetic BMC both still pass;
# div.S/rem.S's own tohost-based assertions still pass on their own merits
# too). It is a genuine, pre-existing defect in test/monitor.v itself
# (tracked, generated, never hand-edited per CLAUDE.md invariant 7):
# monitor_insn_div/monitor_insn_rem compute their spec_rd_wdata as
#   rvfi_rs2_rdata == 32'b0 ? {32{1'b1}} :
#   <overflow special case, also an unsized unsigned literal> :
#   $signed(rvfi_rs1_rdata) / $signed(rvfi_rs2_rdata);
# Per IEEE 1800 ternary sign-context rules, mixing an unsigned literal
# branch ({32{1'b1}}) with a $signed(...)/$signed(...) branch makes the
# *whole* ternary evaluate unsigned, silently downgrading the division
# itself to unsigned — confirmed by isolated reproduction under both
# iverilog and yosys/write_cxxrtl (both compile it to an unsigned div/mod
# cell), so this is not a quirk of either simulator, and DIVU/REMU (whose
# spec has no $signed() at all) are unaffected. It only shows up for
# negative operands, which is exactly what div.S/rem.S exercise. Not
# fixable from this repo's side without hand-editing test/monitor.v, which
# CLAUDE.md forbids; regenerating from a different riscv-formal pin might
# or might not carry a fix and is out of this ticket's scope (ADR-0013 pin
# bumps are their own deliberate action). Flagged for the architect as
# DECISION NEEDED in the JEF-628 PR.
div.S
rem.S
